{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["He shall not defile himself for the dead among his people — a man among the people of the priests shall not defile himself for a human corpse. Like: ״בתולה מעמיו יקח אשה״ — but had it been written לעמיו it would imply: he shall not defile himself לעמיו, as it is written: ״לנפש לא יטמא״. לאחיו ולאחותו לא יטמא להם — and [the phrase] בעמיו is not said of them. Also one may interpret: for a dead person found among his people he shall not defile himself."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The comment argues that בעמיו attaches to איש ('a man among his people, i.e., the priests'), not to לנפש ('a corpse among his people'); Rashbam supports this by comparing the construct form בעמיו with the independent לעמיו, and by noting that the list in vv. 2–3 lacks the phrase בעמיו."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:12.535616717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}